When the core and the project tier resolve to one directory, `--tier core` and `--tier project`
both list its records: one directory, two tiers. The vault's config points the core tier at the
directory the project tier's null `path` resolves to.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core: {path: ~/../cwd/vault/specs}
      project: {path: null}
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/rule/0001-keep-it-short.md --
---
type: rule
title: Keep it short
summary: Cut what the reader does not need.
status: accepted
---
-- cmd --
booping specs ls --tier core
booping specs ls --tier project
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
rule/0001  accepted  Cut what the reader does not need.
rule/0001  accepted  Cut what the reader does not need.
-- stderr --
